====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# An [[incorporeal]] and sometimes [[divine]] messenger from a [[deity]], or other divine entity, often depicted in art as a youthful winged figure in flowing robes.
#* {{RQ:Jonson The Sad Shepherd}}
#*: The dear good '''angel''' of the Spring, / The nightingale.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1982|author=Douglas Adams|authorlink=Douglas Adams|title=Life, the Universe and Everything|page=50|text=There seemed to be girls sitting on top of them, or maybe they were meant to be '''angels'''. '''Angels''' are usually represented as wearing more than that, though.}}
# {{lb|en|Abrahamic tradition}} One of the lowest order of such beings, below [[virtue]]s.
# A person having the qualities attributed to angels, such as [[purity]] or [[selflessness]].
#: {{ux|en|Thanks for making me breakfast in bed, you little '''angel'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=John Eligon|title=Michael Brown Spent Last Weeks Grappling With Problems and Promise|work=The New York Times|date=2014-08-25|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/us/michael-brown-spent-last-weeks-grappling-with-lifes-mysteries.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Michael Brown, 18, due to be buried on Monday, was no '''angel''', with public records and interviews with friends and family revealing both problems and promise in his young life.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Attendant [[spirit]]; [[genius]]; [[demon]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|act=V|scene=viii|page=151|column=1|lines=13–14|passage=Diſpaire thy Charme, / And let the '''Angell''' whom thou ſtill haſt ſeru’d / Tell thee, ''Macduffe'' was from his Mothers womb / Vntimely ript.}}
# {{lb|en|possibly|obsolete}} An official (a [[bishop]], or sometimes a [[minister]]) who heads a [[Christian]] [[church]], especially a {{w|Catholic Apostolic Church}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1817|author=Thomas Stackhouse|title=A history of the holy Bible, corrected and improved by G. Gleig|page=504
|passage=An ''apostle'', or '''''angel''''', or ''bishop'', as he is now called, resided with a college of presbyters about him, in every considerable city of the Roman empire; to that '''''angel''''' or ''bishop'', was committed the pastoral care of all the Christian in the city and its suburbs, extending as far on all sides as the jurisdiction of the civil magistrate extended;}}
#* '''1832''', {{w|Edward Irving}}, speech before the Presbytery of London, quoted in '''1862''', Margaret Oliphant, ''The Life of Edward Irving, Minister of the National Scotch Church, London: Illustrated by His Journals and Correspondence'', page 429
#*: {{...}} the head of that Church, in whose place I stand in my Church, and in whose place no other standeth (the elders and deacons have their place, but this belongeth to the '''angel''' or minister of the Church), and the Lord commendeth him for trying {{...}}
#* '''1878''', Edward Miller, ''The History and Doctrines of Irvingism Or of the So-called Catholic and Apostolic Church'', § 9 ''Pastors'', page 50 (discussing the structure of the early Christian church and of the Catholic Apostolic Church):
#*: The second or highest grade consists of the '''Angels''' or Bishops of Churches. Each Church has its '''Angel''', who has (1) the higher supervision and care of all the flock, (2) the supervision and care of the Priests under him, and (3) the care of the Church itself.
# {{lb|en|historical}} An English [[gold]] [[coin]], bearing the figure of the [[archangel]] [[Michael]], circulated between the 15th and 17th centuries, and varying in value from six [[shilling]]s and [[eightpence]] to ten shillings.
#: {{syn|en|angel-noble}}
# {{lb|en|military slang|originally|_|[[Royal Air Force]]}} An [[altitude]], measured in thousands of [[feet]].
#: {{uxi|en|Climb to '''angels''' sixty.|ascend to 60,000 feet}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|dated}} An [[unidentified flying object]] detected by [[air traffic control]] [[radar]].
# {{lb|en|finance}} An [[angel investor]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=OECD|title=Financing High-Growth Firms: The Role of Angel Investors| passage=“Latent” '''angels''' are defined as those who have not invested capital in the past 12 months, although they likely have invested knowledge in the process of reviewing potential investments.}}
# {{lb|en|theater}} The person who [[fund]]s a [[show]].
#: {{synonyms|en|backer}}

